From 248b2d3349b8e4e281dc2840ef922ff7f41aa05d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:36:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] Safarium: right-click menu for extension buttons

Right-click or Control-click an extension's button in the toolbar or the
vertical sidebar for Chrome's extension menu (Options, Manage Extension,
View Web Permissions, site access, Remove), shown as a native NSMenu
built from the extension's menu model. AppKit gives toolbar right-clicks
to Customize Toolbar first, so the toolbar controller watches the
window's clicks, as the tab bar does.

Safarium places extension buttons with Customize Toolbar rather than
Chrome's pinning, so "Pin to Toolbar" becomes "Remove from Toolbar"
(removes the toolbar or sidebar item), and Remove names Safarium.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
